# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Two jobs:
# 1. SECURITY — never let secrets or runtime data into an image layer. `.env` is the important one.
# 2. SPEED/SIZE — keep the context small so `docker compose build` is fast on a small VPS.
#
# Anything the images DO need must stay out of this list: `package.json`, `bun.lock`, `tsconfig*.json`,
# `apps/`, `packages/`, `scripts/`, `docker/`. Removing one of those breaks the build (or worse, the
# image builds but fails at runtime) — `bun run check:hygiene` guards the critical ones.

# ── secrets and local config ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ── version control and editor noise ──────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*~

# ── dependencies: installed inside the image from the lockfile ────────────
node_modules
**/node_modules
.bun

# ── build/test output: produced inside the image ──────────────────────────
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── runtime data: belongs on volumes, never in an image ───────────────────
data
backups
*.log

# ── documentation and tooling not needed at runtime ──────────────────────
docs
CHANGELOG.md
PROMPT.md
README.md
.editorconfig
.prettierignore
prettier.config.js
eslint.config.js
